DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The oowwllll interface provides access to the link layer of the Dallas Semi‐
     conductor 1-Wire from upper layers of the protocol.

     OOWWLLLL__WWRRIITTEE__OONNEE() and OOWWLLLL__WWRRIITTEE__ZZEERROO() writes a one bit or a zero bit re‐
     spectively on the 1-Wire bus.

     OOWWLLLL__RREEAADD__DDAATTAA() reads one bit from the 1-Wire bus.  This is often re‐
     ferred to as a “Read Time Slot” in the 1-Wire device data sheets.

     The OOWWLLLL__RREESSEETT__AANNDD__PPRREESSEENNCCEE() function starts a reset sequence and de‐
     tects if any device(s) are present on the bus.  This is the beginning of
     all 1-Wire transactions.

NNOOTTEESS
     This interface is intended to be used only by the ow(4) device to talk to
     the low-level bus.  By convention, the device that implements this inter‐
     face is called owc(4).  Only devices that implement own(9) should call
     these interfaces.

